---
import Icon from "../Icon.astro";
---

<section class="section container problem-grid" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
  <div>
    <p class="eyebrow section-label">01 / A BETTER SAVE SYSTEM</p>
    <h2 id="problem-title">
      Autosave isn’t
      <br />
      version control.
    </h2>
    <p class="section-copy">
      Games are very good at saving your progress. They’re significantly less
      good at saving the progress you actually wanted.
    </p>
    <p class="section-copy">
      Save Scum gives you restore points instead of a single, constantly
      overwritten state. It can bring back a save you captured earlier—not one
      that was never backed up.
    </p>
    <a class="text-link" href="/guides/game-save-version-control/">
      Meet your save file’s version history <Icon size={16} />
    </a>
  </div>
  <div class="history-comparison">
    <div class="history-old">
      <span class="micro-label">WITHOUT A HISTORY</span>
      <div class="overwrite-chain">
        <span>SAVE</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <span>SAVE</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        <span class="oops">Oops.</span>
      </div>
      <p>One slot. One version. No take-backs.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="history-new">
      <span class="micro-label">
        <Icon name="history" size={14} /> WITH SAVE SCUM
      </span>
      <div
        class="branch-history"
        aria-label="Example save history: three automatic saves, a before-boss checkpoint, and a panic save"
      >
        <span>
          <i></i>10:00
        </span>
        <span>
          <i></i>10:15
        </span>
        <span class="checkpoint-node">
          <i>★</i>Before boss
        </span>
        <span>
          <i></i>11:08
        </span>
        <span class="panic-node">
          <i>!</i>Panic save
        </span>
      </div>
      <p>
        Jump back to the moment you meant to keep.{" "}
        <Icon name="history" size={17} />
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
